# Example 16: Population dynamics - multicellular population simulation
# Shows mutual regulation of multiple cell types within a population (quorum sensing / resource competition)
#
# Two cell types:
#   producer  : continuously synthesizes signal molecules (quorum-sensing signal AI)
#   responder : responds to AI concentration and expresses a reporter gene once a threshold is reached
#
# p_auto constitutively expresses producer; once AI accumulation crosses the threshold, responder's p_quorum is activated.
# This .helix file declares the quorum-sensing threshold via the #quorum bio-instruction annotation,
# targeting reporter (activates reporter-gene expression once AI concentration reaches 5.0).
# HelixLang's single-cell VM uses #gene/#regulate to describe intracellular networks;
# the coupling of the multicellular population (signal diffusion, division, death, drift) is described via the Python API below:

#promoter name=p_auto strength=-0.4
#promoter name=p_quorum strength=0.7

# producer cell: synthesizes signal molecules
#gene name=ai_synth promoter=p_auto
ATG GCT GCT GCT GCT TAA
#end

# responder cell: expresses the reporter gene in response to AI
#gene name=reporter promoter=p_quorum
ATG GGT GGT GGT GGT TAA
#end

#regulate p_auto -> ai_synth strength=+0.8
#regulate p_quorum -> reporter strength=+0.9

# Quorum-sensing instruction: activates reporter when signal-molecule concentration reaches threshold=5.0
# The parser records it as BioInstruction(kind=quorum, target=reporter, params={threshold:5.0})
#quorum target=reporter threshold=5.0

